ui-split-buttons-scale-with-the-layout-keep-the-leading-and-trailing-segments-together-and-le = Split buttons scale with the layout. Keep the leading and trailing segments together, and let the pair wrap below other controls rather than splitting the two segments apart.

ui-each-segment-keeps-a-minimum-48-48dp-target-so-a-32dp-or-40dp-container-still-exposes-a-fu = Each segment keeps a minimum 48 × 48dp target, so a 32dp or 40dp container still exposes a full-size target for both the action and the menu.

ui-activating-the-leading-segment-runs-the-main-action-immediately-and-leaves-the-menu-untouc = Activating the leading segment runs the main action immediately and leaves the menu untouched. Activating the trailing segment opens the menu anchored to the trailing edge, and the menu icon spins to indicate the expanded state.

ui-choosing-a-menu-item-closes-the-menu-and-reports-the-choice-here-pressing-escape-activatin = Choosing a menu item closes the menu and reports the choice here. Pressing Escape, activating the trailing segment again, or clicking outside the menu also closes it.

